+## Local phase 0 changes after the baseline
+
+- **C1:** `model.CanTransition` now owns a centralized acyclic lifecycle graph, enforced inside the same bbolt transaction as state CAS, history append and quota changes. Known-state no-ops remain idempotent; cancellation cannot revert to execution and terminal states cannot change. Explicit forward observation/recovery edges preserve authoritative results after downtime. Exhaustive model/store pairs, randomized sequences and fuzz seeds exercise rejected writes, history, notifications and reservations. Whole C1 remains Partial: public state names and conditional progress limits differ from the plan, and the EKS campaign has not run.
+- **C12:** a checked-in OpenAPI document is embedded and served through authenticated `GET /v1/openapi.json`. Application errors add stable `code` alongside the compatible human-readable `error`; transient store/controller/backend unavailability adds `Retry-After`. Request parsing rejects duplicate/case-mismatched/unknown fields, null values, invalid UTF-8 and ambiguous auth/idempotency headers. Spec-derived route/auth and example checks plus parser fuzzing are local evidence, not a complete schema validator or the full T16 EKS matrix. Whole C12 remains Partial.
+
